---
/**
 * /power-bi: consultancy (the URL is kept for its history), written to the
 * course-page playbook's consultancy variant: the problem and who has it, how
 * it works, how it starts, the price, proof, a paragraph to forward and one
 * action, the free hour. The opening summary carries the buying facts (a free
 * hour on a call, then fixed price, quoted on request).
 *
 * Existing anchors stay valid: situations, deliver, skills, handover,
 * how-the-work-runs, backup, second-opinion, ai (the /ai-fit-for-teams
 * redirect lands here), start, discovery, pricing, ongoing.
 *
 * No consultancy price is a public claim (claims ledger, 28 Oct 2026), and
 * this page never links the essay, which must stay apart from the law-firm
 * study shown here.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Chapter from "../components/Chapter.astro";
import Exhibit from "../components/Exhibit.astro";
import Offer from "../components/Offer.astro";
import RiseHeading from "../components/RiseHeading.astro";
import type { Line } from "../components/RiseHeading.astro";
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import pbiHero from "../assets/photos/DSC08846-Edit_cropped.jpg";
import BookCta from "../components/BookCta.astro";
import { mailtoFor } from "../config/site";

const contactSubject = "Help with our Power BI";
const contactMailto = mailtoFor(contactSubject);
const heroLines: Line[] = ["Help with Power BI", "only one person", { before: "can ", em: "touch", after: "." }];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Power BI and Fabric consultancy for your own reports - burningsuit"
  description="Power BI and Fabric consultancy from Alan Harman-Box: working alongside your team on its own reports and models until they can carry on without outside help. It starts with a free hour on a call."
  ogImage="/social/linkedin-power-bi.png"
  ogImageAlt="Working alongside your Power BI team, beside a field-notebook model diagram"
  ogImageWidth={1200}
  ogImageHeight={627}
  contactSubject={contactSubject}
>
  <Fragment slot="footer-invitation">Tell me about the reporting you're responsible for and the work ahead. I'll give you a straight answer about whether I can help</Fragment>

  <section class="page-hero pbi-hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <RiseHeading as="h1" kind="hero" label="Help with Power BI only one person can touch." lines={heroLines} />
        <p class="lead enter appear-300">This is consultancy, for when the problem is your own reports and models: a report only one person can change, numbers two teams read differently, a system you've inherited without a proper handover. I work alongside your team on the real thing until they can <strong>carry on without me</strong>.</p>
        <p class="hero-sig enter appear-450">It starts with a free hour on a call. The work after that is fixed price, quoted on request.</p>
        <BookCta src="power-bi-hero" mailtoHref={contactMailto} variant="hero" />
        <p class="routes hour-link"><a class="route" href="/hour/">What happens in the free hour?</a></p>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-photo enter appear-300">
        <Picture src={pbiHero} alt="Alan in a red checked overshirt, smiling, in a narrow brick alley" formats={["avif"]} fallbackFormat="webp" widths={[400, 600, 800]} sizes="(min-width: 62rem) 36vw, 100vw" quality={70} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="thread" data-reveal-raw aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <Chapter id="situations" kicker="How it works">
    <p>We start with the real work in front of your team and make room for the learning it needs. Your people do the work, with me alongside, so they understand the choices and can change them later.</p>
    <div class="offer-table">
      <Offer id="deliver" title="Something to deliver">
        <p>Your team has a report or a model to build or change. We work through the decisions behind it, from what a number needs to mean to how the model should calculate it.</p>
        <p>When a result looks wrong, we follow it back through the model together. Finding the cause is useful in its own right; knowing how you found it helps with the next one.</p>
      </Offer>
      <Offer id="skills" title="One person, on their own work">
        <p>Coaching someone on their own reports is consultancy too: the analyst who keeps bouncing off Power BI, or the lead who has inherited the reports. We work on their real work, with their hands on the keyboard, until they can manage without me.</p>
        <p>If you want a course for a group instead, on my own teaching material, <a href="/training/">that's training</a>.</p>
      </Offer>
      <Offer id="handover" title="A system you've inherited">
        <p>A working system and a pile of handover documents don't always leave a team able to look after it. We trace how the numbers get from the source data to the reports people use, then practise making and checking changes.</p>
        <p>This can happen alongside an outside build, or after the handover.</p>
      </Offer>
    </div>
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter id="how-the-work-runs" kicker="How the sessions run">
    <p>We meet regularly, and you bring the part you're stuck on. Together we try things, check what happens and talk through the reasoning. We can work in your own systems where your data rules allow it, or on examples that reproduce the same problem, so access to live data isn't essential.</p>
    <p>Between sessions, people have time to apply what we've done. An example can make sense while we look at it together, and then the real data turns out to have a complication. We pick that up next time.</p>
    <p>From the first session, your people do the work. As they need me less, we agree less time, and we stop when it stops being useful.</p>
    <Offer id="backup" title="Somewhere to bring the next question">
      <p>Regular time for questions can sit alongside that work, with email between calls. We agree how much time to set aside, and review it as the team needs less help.</p>
    </Offer>
    <p>The <a href="/work/contact-centre/">contact-centre case study</a> shows how this helped a team lead build her own reporting and keep it going.</p>
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter id="second-opinion" kicker="Support for the person leading it" aside="No one person has to understand the full stack to every level of detail.">
    <p>If you're responsible for the reporting but not the one building it, you get someone to think it through with. Asked to sign off an architecture proposal? I'll help you work out what it would mean for the people who have to run it. I'll also say so if a new model won't fix the problem, or a clever addition will leave the team more to maintain than it's worth.</p>
    <p>We can look at what a new hire needs to know, whether the team is ready to take over a system, and where too much depends on one person.</p>
    <p>A regular conversation of your own can sit alongside the team's sessions, or be arranged on its own.</p>
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter id="ai" kicker="AI in the work">
    <p>If your team is using Copilot or an AI agent on its own reports, we can open up a piece of that work and go through it together. A measure can run without an error and still answer the wrong question. That's the part I want the team to be able to spot.</p>
    <p>We work out which parts to hand over, what the tool can see, and how people will check what comes back: reading the calculation, knowing what the number is meant to represent, and what to try when the two don't agree.</p>
    <p>Every piece of work is a stack of decisions. Hand a problem to AI without naming those decisions, and it makes them for you, and a tool can't take responsibility for a decision.</p>
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter id="start" kicker="How it starts">
    <p>With a free hour on a call. Tell me about the reporting, the team and what you're trying to do. By the end of the hour, you'll know what kind of problem it is and what a sensible next step looks like, whether or not that involves me.</p>
    <Offer id="discovery" title="Working out what's needed">
      <p>Sometimes the hour shows that we need to understand the work better before agreeing what to do. That time is part of the quote, not something you buy separately.</p>
    </Offer>
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter id="pricing" kicker="What it costs">
    <p>Consultancy is fixed price. No two pieces of work are the same, so there's no price list. After the free hour, I'll quote one fixed price for the whole piece of work, including the sessions, my preparation and support between sessions, and any time needed first to understand the problem. It's written so you can put it to whoever signs it off.</p>
    <p id="ongoing">If you'd like me around while the work carries on, I'll quote for ongoing support a month at a time instead. We reduce it as the team needs less, and it stops when it stops being useful.</p>
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter id="proof" kicker="In practice">
    <Exhibit tab="Following a wrong number" caption="From the law-firm case study · an international law firm's data team">
      <p>During handover, a year-to-date number looked wrong. With me alongside, the team traced it down through the reporting and through the gold, silver and bronze layers of their data (from ready for reports back to raw) to a stored procedure. The source was year-opening values that a separate app wrote into specific rows. By handover, the team was tracing wrong numbers like this themselves.</p>
      <div class="routes"><a class="route" href="/work/law-firm/">Read the law-firm story</a><a class="route" href="/work/">All four case studies</a></div>
    </Exhibit>
    <p>The case studies are anonymised. I don't name a client without their written permission.</p>
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter id="forward" kicker="To send to your manager">
    {/* The paragraph to forward: it stands on its own when pasted into an
        email to whoever signs the work off. */}
    <p>burningsuit works alongside a team on its own Power BI reports and models, for teams whose reporting depends on one person, or who have inherited a system they need to understand. The team ends up able to carry on without outside help. It starts with a free hour on a call; the work after that is fixed price, quoted on request. To book the free hour: https://burningsuit.co.uk/hour/</p>
  </Chapter>

  <section class="cta-band" aria-label="Book an hour">
    <div class="wrap"><BookCta src="power-bi-pricing" mailtoHref={contactMailto}>Bring the reporting question you're working on. We'll spend an hour on a useful starting point, and the call is free.</BookCta></div>
  </section>

  <div class="thread thread-end" data-reveal-raw aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="talk-spacer"></div>
</BaseLayout>
